id: pm-5mstyv
title: CodeFactor reports zizmor dangerous-triggers on release-reliability.yml's workflow_run trigger as a new critical issue on every PR that touches a workflow
description: "CodeFactor's check on PR #1772 (and on Dependabot PR #1771) failed with one critical issue: zizmor rule dangerous-triggers at .github/workflows/release-reliability.yml line 4, 'workflow_run is almost always used insecurely'. Neither PR changed that file; CodeFactor re-runs zizmor over the workflow set whenever a PR touches any workflow, so every Actions pin update hits it. The trigger is deliberate and already hardened: the job runs only for runs on the default branch (head_branch guard), checks out the default branch rather than the triggering run's code, keeps persist-credentials false, grants only contents/actions/issues read, and downloads no artifact from the triggering run. Fix: record that justification beside the trigger with zizmor's inline suppression so the finding is closed at its source with the reason, instead of being re-reported on unrelated PRs. Duplicate check: searched CodeFactor workflow security finding hosted analysis workflow trigger; pm-92if owns CodeFactor code findings, nothing owns this workflow rule."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: "area:ci",codefactor,security,supply-chain
created_at: "2026-11-23T10:04:05.325Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-23T11:27:13.106Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-23T10:55:49.538Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-23T10:55:49.538Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 15
acceptance_criteria: release-reliability.yml carries a zizmor dangerous-triggers suppression on the workflow_run trigger with the hardening rationale beside it; CodeFactor reports no new issue for PR #1772's final head
parent: pm-92if
risk: low
confidence: medium
resolution: "release-reliability.yml carries '# zizmor: ignore[dangerous-triggers]' on its workflow_run trigger, with the hardening rationale (default-branch runs only, default-branch checkout, unpersisted credentials, read-only permissions, no triggering-run artifacts) in a comment beside it."
expected_result: CodeFactor reports no new issue for PR #1772
actual_result: "CodeFactor failed on 79ae15305 with the dangerous-triggers finding and succeeded on c7d07d1e1, the first head with the suppression; release-reliability.spec.ts and collect-nightly-reliability.spec.ts still parse the workflow (69 tests pass)"
files[1]{path,scope}:
  .github/workflows/release-reliability.yml,project
tests[1]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/scripts/release/release-reliability.spec.ts tests/unit/scripts/release/collect-nightly-reliability.spec.ts,project,"harness:claude-code","2026-11-23T10:16:10.041Z",local_mutation,fix/extension-harness-admission-parity
close_reason: A PR that touches a workflow no longer fails CodeFactor on the hardened workflow_run trigger
escape_class: scanner_finding
